// EXPECT-DIAG: E069
// EXPECT-DIAG: cycle: A -> B -> A
// Regression test: an ARRAY of a struct still contains that struct by
// value -- `B[2]` holds two full copies of `B` directly inside `A`, the
// same as a plain `b: B` field would, just twice over. An array field must
// therefore be unwrapped to its element type when building the by-value
// containment graph, exactly like a plain struct field is (TYPE-001, see
// fail_mutual_struct_cycle.tr for the non-array version of this same A/B
// cycle). Before this unwrapping existed in checkStructLayoutAcyclicity(),
// an array-mediated cycle like this one would have been invisible to a
// naive "is this field's type directly a known struct name" check.

struct A {
    bs: B[2]
}

struct B {
    a: A
}

fn main(): int {
    return 0;
}
